  "root_cause": "Checksum-identical MNIST inputs enter exact density-matrix simulation. Linux/x86 and macOS/ARM feature arrays first differ at 5e-17 to 7e-16 and remain within 6.44e-15. Those feature changes alone alter no decisions. The validation-selected multinomial LogisticRegression uses L-BFGS with tol=1e-4 on feature designs with condition numbers 1.57e5 to 6.41e5. Platform BLAS and last-bit inputs therefore stop on different, nearly equivalent iterates, producing 22 changed validation/test decisions across 6000 evaluated seed-example pairs. Re-fitting the same qBraid arrays on macOS changes the iterate again; tightening tol stabilizes decisions but changes the checksum-frozen prediction path and is therefore not a permitted reproduction fix.",
